<h2 id="typography">Typography</h2>
<p class="kh-reference-display">Make it make sense.</p>
{% markdown %}
Anton 400 is the display voice. IBM Plex Sans 400/600 handles reading and interfaces; Plex Mono 400 handles code and metadata. Copy stays sentence case; display uppercase is CSS. The [design guide](/style-guide/design/#type) describes the hierarchy and [font assets](#font-variations) lists loaded faces.

Page-title typography is selected by the page family, not by adding a heavier font weight. Standard titles grow to 4.5rem; utility, note and photo titles are smaller. Long-form reading uses 18px and about 62ch, reducing to 17px on small screens.
{% endmarkdown %}
<h3 id="heading-classes">Heading classes and document outline</h3>
{% markdown %}
`.kh-text-heading--1`, `--2` and `--3` are retained type utilities. They do not change a heading's semantic level. Use one page `h1`, then choose heading levels for the document outline. These examples use `h3` because they sit under this reference's Typography section; they demonstrate utility classes, not additional page titles.
{% endmarkdown %}
