<h2 id="datasheet">Shared structure</h2>
<span id="datasheet-register" aria-hidden="true"></span>
{% markdown %}
The datasheet class names remain stable. Their current presentation uses cobalt rules, open lists and restrained panels. Decorative section numbers are retired from indexes; stable project references and ordered instructions still carry meaningful numbers.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-section-head">
  <h3>Recent writing</h3>
  <span class="kh-meta">Newest first</span>
</div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<h3 id="panels">Panels</h3>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-panel">
  <div class="kh-panel__row">
    <div class="kh-panel__cell"><span class="kh-panel__label">Place</span>Bonn, Germany</div>
    <div class="kh-panel__cell"><span class="kh-panel__label">Practice</span>Platforms, content and audiences</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-panel__row">
    <div class="kh-panel__cell"><span class="kh-panel__label">Purpose</span>Group related facts with a shared boundary.</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% markdown %}
- `.kh-section-head` aligns a heading and supporting metadata; it can wrap.
- `.kh-panel` groups related rows on white with a 2px ink frame and a 4px cobalt offset shadow. Internal rules stay light so the values remain easy to scan. `.kh-panel__row` and `.kh-panel__cell` supply the structure; `.kh-panel__label` names a value in uppercase cobalt mono. Direct navigation links use Sans 600. Keep the cells upright and preserve wrapping at narrow widths.
- Use [tables](#tables) when comparison requires column headings. A panel is not a substitute for table semantics.
- Navigation, entry footers and bylines are repeated chrome. Put `data-pagefind-ignore` on the wrapper so their content does not leak into Pagefind or embeddings.

Sources: `_kh-datasheet.scss` for the stable primitives; `_kh-cartridge-system.scss` for current surfaces and rules. Do not add an empty left column merely to indent an introduction.
{% endmarkdown %}

