<h2 id="micro-copy">Labels and micro-copy</h2>
{% markdown %}
Use the [interface vocabulary](/style-guide/editorial/#interface-vocabulary) for destination names and deliberate context-specific labels. Keep labels in sentence case; descriptions should add information rather than repeat the heading.

`.kh-cartridge-kicker`, `.kh-meta` and `.kh-panel__label` are supporting labels. They must remain readable without hover. Put an explanation next to a data mark when its meaning would otherwise depend on a tooltip. Preserve proper names and acronyms; do not author all-caps text just because its display style is uppercase.
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="buttons">Buttons and links</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-cluster"><a class="kh-button" href="/work/">Explore the work</a>
  <button class="kh-button" type="button">Example action</button>
  <button class="kh-button" type="button" disabled>Unavailable action</button>
</div>
<p><a href="/all/">Ordinary navigation stays a link ↗</a></p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% markdown %}
Buttons use Plex Sans 600, white on cobalt, square corners and at least 44px height. Hover/focus uses ink; keyboard focus has an ink outline and white inner ring. Resize or use a keyboard to inspect the live controls. The example action has no side effect; the disabled example uses the native disabled state.

| Contract | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `.kh-button` on an `a` with `href` | Navigation to a real destination |
| `.kh-button` on `button type="button"` | An action implemented by its owner |
| `button type="submit"` | Submits the surrounding form |
| `disabled` | A native unavailable action; supply surrounding explanation when needed |
| `aria-label` | Required when an icon or hidden text would otherwise leave the control unnamed |

The retained `--primary` and `--sm` class names appear in older content. The cartridge rule defines the common button presentation; do not assume those names provide a new hierarchy or smaller target. The old button-colour custom properties are overridden by the cartridge styling. Add a scoped, documented component modifier when a new variant is actually needed.

Sources: `index.scss` and `_kh-cartridge-system.scss`. Search-specific label/icon spans are documented under [search forms](#search-form).
{% endmarkdown %}

