<h2 id="note-boxes">Note boxes</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<aside class="kh-note-box"><span class="kh-note-box__label">Update</span>A short correction that changes how the surrounding text should be read.</aside>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<aside class="kh-note-box"><span class="kh-note-box__label">Context</span>
  <p>A note may contain more than one block when the structure helps.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A scoped qualification.</li>
    <li>A link to the <a href="/style-guide/editorial/">editorial guidance</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</aside>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Use <code>aside</code> for contextual content, a concise summary or a correction; keep ordinary paragraphs outside boxes. Use a short label such as “Update” or “Context”. The current treatment is a cobalt left rule and a lighter surface. Sources: <code>index.scss</code> and <code>_kh-cartridge-system.scss</code>; editorial guidance: <a href="/style-guide/editorial/#note-boxes">note boxes</a>.</p>

<span id="margin-notes-and-pull-quotes" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="margin-notes">Margin notes and pull-quotes</h2>
{% markdown %}
Author using paired shortcodes inside a Markdown block. They render inline Markdown, so links, emphasis, code and `--` punctuation work. Keep each aside to one or two sentences, with no blank paragraphs inside the shortcode.

```njk
{% raw %}{% marginnote %}Supporting detail with a [source](/colophon/).{% endmarginnote %}
{% pullquote %}Keep the evidence near the claim.{% endpullquote %}{% endraw %}
```

A margin note is additional content: it stays in the accessibility tree and search. A pull-quote repeats a phrase from the body: the shortcode adds `aria-hidden="true"` and `data-pagefind-ignore`. **Unique information must never exist only in a pull-quote.**

At 1300px and above, article notes float into the right margin and the reading measure adjusts. Below that and in print they return to the flow. The reference previews below deliberately show the in-flow form; inspect an article with notes to verify the wide-margin behaviour.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-reference-asides">
  <aside class="kh-marginnote">Supporting context, including a <a href="/colophon/">source link</a>.</aside>
  <p>The main argument remains readable on its own.</p>
</div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-reference-asides">
  <p>Keep the evidence near the claim.</p>
  <aside class="kh-pullquote" aria-hidden="true" data-pagefind-ignore>Keep the evidence near the claim.</aside>
</div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<p>Sources: shortcode registration in <code>config/eleventy/markdown.js</code>; layout, float arithmetic and print rules in <code>_kh-content.scss</code>. Prefer the shortcodes to hand-written markup so the accessibility/search markers remain intact.</p>

