<span id="inline-code" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="code-blocks" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="code">Code and live demos</h2>
{% markdown %}
Use fenced Markdown with a language identifier. Inline code can wrap when needed; long blocks contain their own overflow. Source text must not force the entire page sideways.

```scss
.example {
  color: var(--kh-cart-ink);
}
```

<h3 id="code-live-demo-codeanddemo-shortcode">The paired codeAndDemo shortcode</h3>

Place it **outside** a Markdown block. Its body becomes both escaped source and live HTML:

```njk
{% raw %}{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<p>A small example with <code>inline code</code>.</p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}{% endraw %}
```
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<p>A small example with <code>inline code</code>.</p>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% markdown %}
The shortcode adds `.kh-demo` with `data-pagefind-ignore`, a `pre/code` pane, and `.kh-demo__live`. Samples therefore stay out of the site's keyword and semantic indexes. Live markup still needs unique IDs, correct headings and harmless actions. Prefer local placeholders to loading third-party embeds. Never submit sample feedback to the live service.

Sources: `config/eleventy/markdown.js` and `.kh-demo` in `_kh-content.scss`. To show Nunjucks tags rather than execute them, wrap the example in a Nunjucks `raw` block.
{% endmarkdown %}

