<h2 id="figures">Figures and images</h2>
{% markdown %}
Put source files in `src/site/images/blog/`; entry frontmatter uses `/blog/filename.ext`. The hero image and the social card are separate mechanisms. Provide descriptive alt text, a useful caption and the correct credit. Ken’s photos use `credit: "Own work."` with location context in the caption.

The image transform can produce a `<picture>` wrapper. In grids and flex layouts, target that direct child as well as the image. Use the original colours of photographs, diagrams and project screenshots. A wide image may break the reading measure, but it must not break the viewport.

The live feedback counter is a remote image and must retain `eleventy:ignore`. A raster still pointing to `/images/` in production, or a `/.11ty/image/` URL in production HTML, is a failed transform; the build checks catch both cases.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<figure>
  <img src="/images/cartridge-pattern.svg" alt="Sparse blue, yellow, green, red and black geometric marks: zigzag, paired strokes, outlined square, wavy line, dotted rule, circle and triangle." width="520" height="160" loading="lazy" eleventy:ignore>
  <figcaption class="kh-figure__caption">Current cover-margin pattern, drawn for this site. The serrated boundaries use the separate <code>cartridge-edge.svg</code> mask.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}

<h3 id="figure-contexts">Prose figures, page figures and wide media</h3>
{% markdown %}
Use a plain `figure` inside `.kh-content`. `.kh-figure` is the page-level figure grid; content rules deliberately neutralise that grid when it is nested inside prose. The live example above is a prose figure. A page-level layout can use:

```html
<figure class="kh-figure">
  <img class="kh-figure__image" src="/images/cartridge-pattern.svg" width="520" height="160" alt="Describe the meaningful image.">
  <figcaption class="kh-figure__caption">Caption and credit.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

For a deliberate reading-column escape, use `figure class="kh-bleed-out"` and inspect it in the actual article layout. Its left bleed begins at 767px and assumes available space beside the reading column; a general documentation panel is not that context. Preserve captions and alternative text at every width.

The transform may replace `img` with `picture`. Grid areas and overlap layouts must target the direct `picture` wrapper as well as an untransformed image. Sources: `_kh-content.scss`, `index.scss`, and the [image pipeline notes](/style-guide/editorial/#images).
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="tables">Tables</h2>
{% markdown %}
`.kh-table--spec` supplies column boundaries and current cobalt headers. Use real `table`, `thead`, `tbody`, `th` and `td` elements when readers compare records. Give headers `scope="col"` or `scope="row"`; use a caption when the surrounding heading does not name the table.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-table-scroll">
  <table class="kh-table--spec">
    <caption>Example project record</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Project</th>
        <th scope="col">Year</th>
        <th scope="col">Organization</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Shared design system</th>
        <td>2026</td>
        <td>UNDRR</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Visual Framework</th>
        <td>2019</td>
        <td>EMBL</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
<h3 id="spec-table">Stacking versus scrolling</h3>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<div class="kh-table-scroll">
  <table class="kh-table--spec kh-table--stack">
    <caption>Example compact record</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Project</th>
        <th scope="col">Year</th>
        <th scope="col">Organization</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/work/">Platform recovery</a></td>
