<span id="the-marks" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="data-marks">Data marks</h2>
{% markdown %}
These build-time marks carry text equivalents and links; they must remain meaningful with CSS disabled. They are not interchangeable with headline metric tiles.

| Pattern | Implementation | Meaning and constraint |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Publishing timeline / pulse | `partials/pulse-strip.njk`; `pulseMonths` filter | Dated publishing activity, with links and collapsed empty periods; not a decorative progress bar |
| Neighbour sequence | `partials/sequence-mark.njk`; `neighbourhood` filter | This entry and chronological neighbours; retained in the entry-foot assembly where selected by layout data |
| Reading-length gauge | `partials/length-gauge.njk`; `lengthFrame` filter | Position among the comparison corpus; keep the word count, percentile and median explanation |
| Topic tally | `topicTally` filter in the article layout | Number of entries sharing a topic; preserve the visible count |

<h3 id="entry-type-key">Entry-type key</h3>

Where type is encoded as a mark, preserve shape, colour and the text equivalent together. Avoid inventing new abbreviations in a legend. SVGs may carry their own presentation colours; check the actual generated mark rather than assuming every SVG consumes a CSS token. The current article places its publishing timeline at the end, not in the opening masthead.

Sources: `_kh-dataviz.scss`, `config/eleventy/` filters, `partials/entry-foot.njk` and the individual partials. Add `data-pagefind-ignore` to navigation that repeats other entries' titles.
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="layout">Layout primitives</h2>
{% markdown %}
The shell and colour fields span the viewport. Header, homepage and footer content share a centred 72rem measure with at least 2rem desktop gutters and 1rem mobile gutters. Ordinary page layouts remain capped at 76rem; `.kh-content` defaults to 70ch and article prose to about 62ch. `.kh-content--wide` removes the generic content measure, not every enclosing page constraint.

<h3 id="breakpoints">Breakpoints</h3>

| Sass token | Value | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `$kh-breakpoint--sm` / `--sm-down` | 600px / 599px | Small-screen boundary |
| `$kh-breakpoint--md` / `--md-down` | 846px / 845px | Main layout changes |
| `$kh-breakpoint--lg` / `--lg-down` | 1024px / 1023px | Larger grid spacing |
| `$kh-breakpoint--xl` | 1300px | Wide reading layouts and margin notes |

Use the `-down` partner for max-width rules so adjacent ranges do not both match the same boundary pixel. Source: `_settings.scss`.
{% endmarkdown %}
