<h3 id="full-bleed-kh-u-fullbleed">Full-width fields and retained bleed hooks</h3>

Current cover/writing/footer fields use full-width blocks with fluid `--kh-cart-gutter` padding. Keep content centred and extend decorative background layers, instead of widening paragraphs. The full-width regression check covers these fields at mobile and wide viewports. This is page-level markup in the full-width homepage main, not a breakout applied inside an article:

```html
<section class="kh-cartridge-writing" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
  <div class="kh-cartridge-section-head">
    <h2 id="writing-title">Ideas in circulation</h2>
    <a href="/all/">All writing</a>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-datasheet-list">
    <!-- Render the shared post-summary partial for each entry. -->
  </div>
</section>
```

`.kh-u-fullbleed` remains a legacy pseudo-element helper using viewport arithmetic. It is not the current shell's implementation and should not be the starting point for a new section. `.kh-bleed-out` remains available for wide figures; its left-side escape depends on the surrounding layout and must be checked at real widths.

Sources: `index.scss`, `_kh-cartridge.scss`, `_kh-cartridge-system.scss`. See the [design guide composition](/style-guide/design/#composition) before adding a new page composition.
{% endmarkdown %}

<h2 id="pager">Pager and navigation states</h2>
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<nav class="kh-pager" aria-label="Pagination example">
  <ul class="kh-pager__list">
    <li><a href="/all/" class="kh-pager__link">← Newer</a></li>
    <li><a href="/all/" class="kh-pager__link">1</a></li>
    <li><a href="#pager" class="kh-pager__link kh-pager__link--current" aria-current="page">2</a></li>
    <li><a href="/all/3/" class="kh-pager__link">3</a></li>
    <li><a href="/all/3/" class="kh-pager__link">Older →</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% markdown %}
Use the shared `partials/pager.njk` for actual collections. It receives Eleventy's pagination object plus optional `pagerLabel`, `pagerNewer` and `pagerOlder`, and suppresses itself when only one page exists. The current link carries `.kh-pager__link--current` and `aria-current="page"`; newer/older destinations remain real links. The example above labels its own local state, not the page's global navigation.

The primary navigation has two strengths: `.kh-navigation__link--active` marks the exact page; `--section` identifies a parent section. Only exact-page links receive `aria-current`. Writing stays a parent on paginated `/all/` routes. Label destinations using the [interface vocabulary](/style-guide/editorial/#interface-vocabulary).

Sources: `partials/pager.njk`, `layouts/base.njk`, `_kh-datasheet.scss`, `index.scss` and `_kh-cartridge.scss`.
{% endmarkdown %}

<span id="spacing-utilities" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="content-width" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="spacing">Spacing utilities</h2>
{% markdown %}
Prefer a component's layout/gap before adding per-child offsets. The existing utilities are explicit hooks, not a generated universal scale: do not assume a new numeric suffix exists.

| Class | Property | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `.kh-u-margin__bottom--200` | margin-bottom | 0.5rem |
| `.kh-u-margin__bottom--600` | margin-bottom | 1.5rem |
| `.kh-u-margin__top--1200` | margin-top | 3rem |
| `.kh-u-padding__bottom--200` | padding-bottom | 0.75rem |
| `.kh-u-padding__bottom--400` | padding-bottom | 1rem |
| `.kh-u-padding__top--500` | padding-top | 1.5rem |
| `.kh-u-padding__top--600` | padding-top | 2rem |
| `.kh-u-padding__top--800` | padding-top | 3rem |

`--kh-stack-margin--custom` is the stack's intentional spacing override; the ordinary `--kh-stack-margin` is set/reset by the stack rules; `--kh-page-grid-gap` supplies the shared gap (1rem, rising to 2rem at 1024px). A component-specific gap can override that default. Check the cascade before stacking a utility onto an existing margin. Sources: `index.scss` and `_kh-content.scss`.
{% endmarkdown %}

