<span id="markup" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="design-details" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="feedback-toast">Feedback and confirmation toast</h2>
{% markdown %}
The real feedback action and counter are assembled by `partials/feedback.njk`. Keep the action's service URL and `rel="nofollow"`; keep the live remote SVG counter's `eleventy:ignore` so the build never freezes or rasterises it. Use a grammar-neutral label because its count is unknown at build time. The action uses the shared `.kh-button` treatment: square cobalt fill, white Plex Sans 600 text, a 44px minimum target, ink hover and visible keyboard focus. `.kh-feedback__action` removes the button’s outer margin; visiting the service must not change its appearance.

<h3 id="how-it-works">Fragment-driven confirmation</h3>

The service redirects back to `#thanks`. That fragment targets the hidden `.kh-feedback-thanks` element; CSS displays the fixed banner, starts the timer and dismisses it after about 15 seconds. The production element carries `aria-live="polite"`. This pattern uses no feedback-submission JavaScript.
{% endmarkdown %}
{% codeAndDemo 'html' %}
<p class="kh-meta">Was this useful?</p>
<a class="kh-button kh-feedback__action" href="#guide-feedback-toast"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128077;&nbsp;</span> This was useful</a>
{% endcodeAndDemo %}
{% markdown %}
The demo deliberately targets a local example ID and never calls the service. Re-trigger by navigating away from its fragment and back. Check the announcement and focus experience as well as the visual banner. Source: `index.scss` (`.kh-feedback-thanks`, `kh-banner-in`, `kh-banner-out`, `kh-timer`) and the [feedback implementation article](/posts/20260220-feedback-buttons-cgi-pattern/).
{% endmarkdown %}

<span id="atmospheric-background-dappled-light" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="dappled-light">Earlier visual treatments</h2>
<p>The graph paper, full-site light effect and ruled numbered mastheads are retired from the shared shell. The <a href="/posts/sunlit-dappled-light-effect/">lighting article</a> and <a href="/posts/20250904-switching-to-recursive/">font history</a> preserve the experiments. The <a href="/design-lab/megadrive/">proposal board</a> preserves the design directions. Retaining an archive does not make every archived treatment a current default. Social-sharing cards use the current palette and type in their own fixed-size, noindex document.</p>

<p>Decorative backgrounds use near-white paper, angled colour fields and small sawtooth edges. The writing-field edge and role ribbon use <code>cartridge-edge.svg</code> as a repeated mask; <code>cartridge-pattern.svg</code> supplies sparse cover marks. Patterns belong in margins and section boundaries, with upright content and enough clear space for focus rings.</p>

<span id="accessibility-patterns" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility contracts</h2>
<h3 id="skip-link">Skip link</h3>
{% markdown %}
The base layout's first link points to `#main-content`. `.kh-u-sr-only.kh-skip-link` hides it visually until keyboard focus; focus restores the size and clip so it is usable. Keep one real target in the layout rather than inserting competing demo IDs.

<h3 id="screen-reader-only">Visually hidden text</h3>

`.kh-u-sr-only` keeps content in the accessibility tree. `aria-hidden="true"` removes content from it. They are not alternatives: use the former for an accessible label, the latter for genuinely redundant decoration. Pull-quotes also carry `data-pagefind-ignore` because they repeat body text.

<h3 id="focus-indicators">Focus and control states</h3>

Shared controls use an ink outline and white inner ring. Check links and buttons on paper, cobalt and green, alongside selected, hovered, disabled and invalid states. Keep visible labels, unique IDs and native control semantics. Primary actions are at least 44px; inputs are at least 48px high.

<h3 id="css-toggle">CSS-off mode</h3>

Every custom rule belongs inside `body:has(#kh-css-toggle:checked)`. The footer owns the real checked checkbox. Do not add a second checkbox with that ID, or put inline presentation styles into a demo that would survive CSS-off. Source order, text alternatives and real links must continue to work without styling.

<h3 id="reduced-motion">Motion and enlarged text</h3>

New motion must honour `prefers-reduced-motion`. Review existing animated components on their own merits; a semantic pattern does not guarantee its animation is already compliant. Test at 200% text sizing: cover text must reflow, and clipping is only for decoration. The overflow checker specifically checks enlarged cover text as well as document width.

<h3 id="high-contrast">Contrast and non-colour meaning</h3>

Use the [palette's measured combinations](/style-guide/design/#palette). Keep charts' text keys and shape cues. Check forced-colour/high-contrast modes in the actual component; do not infer support solely from the ordinary screenshot. Alt text, captions and print content remain part of the component contract.
{% endmarkdown %}

<span id="utility-classes" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="color" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="links" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="navigation" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="color-properties" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="layout-properties" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="utilities">Utilities, tokens and implementation</h2>
<h3 id="visibility">Visibility utilities</h3>
{% markdown %}
These describe the actual rules in `index.scss`, including legacy naming. Do not infer a breakpoint from a class name.

| Class | Current behaviour |
| --- | --- |
| `.kh-u-show-for-mobile-only` | Screen widths below 600px |
| `.kh-u-show-for-medium-up` | Visible from 600px upward; despite its name, the hide rule ends at 599px |
| `.kh-u-show-for-medium-only` | 846–1023px |
| `.kh-u-show-for-large` | 1024px and above |
| `.kh-u-show-for-print-only`, `.kh-u-for-print-only` | Hidden on screen, available in print |
| `.kh-u-do-not-print` | Hidden in print |
| `.kh-u-sr-only` | Visually hidden; available to assistive technology |

Do not use a visibility utility to hide the only navigation at a viewport width. Preserve the legacy names until an intentional migration; document their behaviour here.

<h3 id="text">Text, link and navigation hooks</h3>

| Hook | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| `.kh-u-text--nowrap` | Prevents wrapping; use only when the content can still fit at enlarged text sizes |
| `.kh-u-text-color--grey` | Consumes `--kh-color--grey`, mapped to muted ink by the theme |
| `.kh-link` | Standalone link styling outside ordinary `.kh-content` prose |
| `.kh-navigation`, `__list`, `__item`, `__link` | Navigation structure; active/section state described under [Pager](#pager) |
| `.ken-link--print` | Print wrapper that exposes link destinations |

<h3 id="print">Print</h3>

Keep reading order and captions useful when colour/backgrounds disappear. Screen-only controls use `.kh-u-do-not-print`; print-only contact content uses the existing print utilities. Margin notes return to the flow. Check the CV's print action, a long article, a table and a figure after changing shared typography or widths.

<h3 id="css-custom-properties-reference">Current token reference</h3>

| Property or group | Current role/value |
| --- | --- |
| `--kh-cart-paper` / `--kh-cart-ink` | `#faf9f5` / `#151515` |
| `--kh-cart-blue` / `--kh-cart-yellow` | `#173ebc` / `#f6d92f` |
| `--kh-cart-red` / `--kh-cart-green` | `#ee3e35` / `#007c55` |
| `--kh-ground` | Alias of paper |
| `--kh-color--blue`, `--kh-color--apparatus` | Aliases of cobalt |
| `--kh-color--sun` | Yellow in the cartridge system; the name is retained for compatibility |
| `--kh-color--sun--deep`, `--kh-color--yellow--dark` | Cobalt in the cartridge system |
| `--kh-ink-muted`, `--kh-color--grey` | `#5b5e5a` muted ink |
| `--kh-color--visited` | `#563d82` for visited reading links |
| `--kh-panel-bg` | `#ffffff` |
| `--kh-rule`, `--kh-rule--strong` | Ink at 20% opacity / solid ink |
| `--kh-cart-gutter` | Fluid outer gutter aligning a 72rem content measure; minimum 2rem, 1rem on mobile |
| `--kh-cart-cut` | Decorative diagonal depth, clamped from 1.5rem to 3.5rem |
| `--kh-page-grid-gap` | 1rem; 2rem from 1024px |
| `--kh-grid-stylized-module--prime` | Legacy 16rem label track, where the layout retains it |
| `--kh-body-width` | Legacy base-shell setting; the cartridge shell overrides it, so it does not control current full-width fields |
| `--kh-font-sans`, `--kh-font-mono` | Self-hosted Plex stacks with system fallbacks |

<h3 id="theming">Component overrides and ownership</h3>

`.kh-box` reads `--kh-box-theme-color--background` and `--kh-box-theme-color--foreground`. Old button-colour properties remain in the base CSS but do not override the cartridge button rule. Prefer a purposeful component modifier to an undocumented inline override. Keep new custom properties declared or provide an intentional fallback; `lint:css-vars` checks unresolved reads.

Layout frontmatter supplies `cartridgeTheme`: `page`, `home`, `article`, `note`, `story`, `photo`, `profile` or `utility`. Base/layout inheritance supplies the body class and display-font preload. Do not repeat a layout's default flag in every post. Standalone lab documents and historical experiments must identify themselves rather than silently becoming alternative site defaults.

| Concern | Source of truth |
| --- | --- |
| Palette, shell, cover and article composition | `src/components/vf-componenet-rollup/_kh-cartridge.scss` |
| Shared controls, page families and guide primitives | `_kh-cartridge-system.scss` in the same directory |
| Content typography, notes, figures and demos | `_kh-content.scss` |
| Retained primitives and utilities | `_kh-datasheet.scss`, `index.scss`, `_settings.scss` |
| Behaviour | The relevant partial/module, not a duplicate controller in this reference |
| Naming and copy | [Editorial guide](/style-guide/editorial/#interface-vocabulary) |

Use `data-pagefind-ignore` for repeated chrome and other entries' titles. Use `noindex` for non-destinations and `kens_status: draft` for reviewable unpublished posts. Keep those exclusions in their existing shared mechanisms.

<h3 id="reference-verification">Verifying a change</h3>

- Check real source markup and at least one production use before documenting a variant.
- Exercise keyboard focus, native disclosures, the local toast, search submission and narrow/wide layouts. Keep examples' actions harmless.
- Check CSS-off, 200% text, print, reduced motion and high-contrast behaviour. A live demo documents a contract; it is not proof of all accessibility states.
- Run `yarn lint:css`, production rendering, `yarn lint:links`, `yarn lint:images`, `yarn lint:css-vars` and `yarn lint:overflow` as appropriate. Run production link/image gates before restarting dev, whose image endpoints differ.
- Keep old section IDs next to the replacement material so shared links remain useful. Update this reference and the design guide with implementation changes.
